---
import BlogArticleShell from '../../../components/BlogArticleShell.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonicalPath = '/blog/kakobuy-tracksuits-pants-spreadsheet-lane-2026';
const publishedISO = '2026-06-17';
---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="Tracksuits & pants on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet: 2026 lane guide | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="A data-backed guide to tracksuits and trousers on kakobuy-cn.com—44 pants rows plus 22 tracksuit cards, Corteiz and Nike clusters, taper/fit QC, and freight for bottom-heavy hauls."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="Tracksuits & pants lane guide: bottoms on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet (2026)"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="17 June 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'Kakobuy Spreadsheet tracksuits',
    'Corteiz Nike tracksuit guide',
    'trousers pants reps 2026',
    'Stone Island pants QC',
    'kakobuy-cn.com pants lane',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    Bottoms are where spreadsheets lie with sizing—same thumbnail, three different inseams, four factories.
    Our <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> indexes <strong>44 trousers/pants rows</strong> and <strong>22 tracksuit rows</strong> in deep pools behind the homepage <a href="/category/pants/">Pants/Shorts</a> shortcut as of <strong>17 June 2026</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>June 2026 snapshot</h2>
  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Pool</th><th scope="col">Rows</th><th scope="col">Top labels</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>trousers-pants</code></td>
          <td>44</td>
          <td>Gallery Dept., Stone Island, Polo Ralph Lauren, Ami Paris, Arc'teryx (3 each)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>tracksuits</code></td>
          <td>22</td>
          <td>Adidas, Corteiz, Gucci, Nike (3 each)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Tracksuit culture rows</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Corteiz</strong>, <strong>Nike</strong>, and <strong>Adidas</strong> lead tracksuit counts—full-zip vs hoodie-set listings vary; confirm top+bottom inclusion in title.
    <strong>Gucci</strong> tracks appear less often but carry heavier branded routing—<a href="/blog/shipping-branded-vs-unbranded-spreadsheet-restrictions/">shipping restrictions</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Trousers &amp; denim-adjacent</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Stone Island</strong> and <strong>Gallery Dept.</strong> dominate pants rows—badge and distressing QC respectively.
    <strong>Arc'teryx</strong> technical pants overlap with <a href="/blog/kakobuy-jackets-outerwear-spreadsheet-lane-2026/">outerwear guide</a> for gorpcore builds.
  </p>

  <h2>Sizing discipline</h2>
  <p>
    Measure waist, rise, and inseam on trousers you own; compare flat-lay listing charts.
    Tracksuit sets may size differently top vs bottom—verify both tags in QC photos.
    Deep-read <a href="/blog/kakobuy-sizing-spreadsheet-apparel/">sizing guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Zipper alignment on track jackets bundled with pants</li>
    <li>Stripe alignment on Adidas-class side seams</li>
    <li>Stone Island badge position on leg or pocket</li>
    <li>Pocket bag depth and stitching on cargo rows</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Freight</h2>
  <p>
    Pants stack densely—good freight citizens vs puffers.
    Pair with hoodies and tees for bracket tuning—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-hoodies-sweatshirts-spreadsheet-lane-2026/">hoodies guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet home</a></strong> → <a href="/category/pants/">Pants</a>.</li>
    <li>Confirm set vs single piece; paste URL.</li>
    <li>QC waist tag and length; reject wrong inseam early.</li>
  </ol>
</BlogArticleShell>
